          "sameLine": false,
          "value": " @target: es2015"
        },
        {
          "type": "Line",
          "position": "before",
          "sameLine": false,
          "value": " A contextual signature S is extracted from a function type T as follows:"
        },
        {
          "type": "Line",
          "position": "before",
          "sameLine": false,
          "value": "      If T is a function type with exactly one call signature, and if that call signature is non- generic, S is that signature."
        },
        {
          "type": "Line",
          "position": "before",
          "sameLine": false,
          "value": "      If T is a union type, let U be the set of element types in T that have call signatures."
        },
        {
          "type": "Line",
          "position": "before",
          "sameLine": false,
          "value": "          If each type in U has exactly one call signature and that call signature is non- generic,"
        },
        {
          "type": "Line",
          "position": "before",
          "sameLine": false,
          "value": "          and if all of the signatures are identical ignoring return types, then S is a signature"
        },
        {
          "type": "Line",
          "position": "before",
          "sameLine": false,
          "value": "          with the same parameters and a union of the return types."
        },
        {
          "type": "Line",
          "position": "before",
          "sameLine": false,
          "value": "      Otherwise, no contextual signature can be extracted from T and S is undefined."
        }
      ]
    },
